# Simple OS – printing and scanning (Control Center → System → Printers & Scanners)
# Built without Recommends, so everything is explicit. Modern printers need no driver: CUPS finds them on the
# network via Avahi (IPP Everywhere/AirPrint), over USB via ipp-usb. Older devices: printer-driver-all
# (HP, Brother, Epson, Samsung …) and the Foomatic PPDs.
cups
cups-client
cups-filters
ghostscript
printer-driver-all
foomatic-db-compressed-ppds
ipp-usb
avahi-daemon
libnss-mdns
# Printer settings; cups-pk-helper: add printers with a password dialog instead of a root terminal;
# -udev sets up printers plugged in via USB without IPP automatically
system-config-printer
system-config-printer-udev
cups-pk-helper
# Scanning: sane-airscan finds network/USB scanners without drivers (eSCL/WSD), simple-scan is the front end
sane-airscan
sane-utils
simple-scan
